4. THE COST OF THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN LOWER a0 -- it makes eta WORSE than standard MOND
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Deep regime: g_obs -> sqrt(a0 g_bar), so at fixed g_obs the predicted mass scales as
  sqrt(a0) and eta scales as sqrt(a0_rival / a0_framework).  Rival = 1.200e-10 (McGaugh+16).
  canonical rho_DE  (cH_Lambda/Z)    sqrt(a0_rival/a0) = 1.1322  (+13.2% on eta)   measured geomean ratio = 1.1272
  alt rho_total     (cH_0/Z)         sqrt(a0_rival/a0) = 1.0300  (+3.0% on eta)   measured geomean ratio = 1.0290
  This is not a rounding detail: the framework's distinctive content IS the coefficient,
  and here the coefficient costs it 13.2% (canonical) / 3.0% (alt).
  Erasing eta by an a0 boost alone needs a0 x eta^2, on the canonical footing:
    median  eta=2.334      -> a0 x 5.45 (= +0.736 dex), i.e. a0 ~ 5.10e-10 -- which the galaxy RAR excludes.
    geomean eta=2.542      -> a0 x 6.46 (= +0.810 dex), i.e. a0 ~ 6.05e-10 -- which the galaxy RAR excludes.

